NEARS-2623 QA — regression-candidate found during regression sweep (pre-existing, unrelated to this diff)
Device: emulator-5554 (Pixel 10 Pro AVD, sdk_gphone16k_arm64), UserApp worktree fix/NEARS-2623-payment-webview-exit-dialog-route
Package: com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_2623_payment_webview_exit_di

Repro (live, this session):
1. Logged in as customer@nears.com. Profile -> Wallet -> Add Fund -> amount "50" -> select "Paypal, not selected" -> tap "Add Fund" (submit).
2. Native InAppBrowserActivity opens (com.pichillilorenzo.flutter_inappwebview_android...) atop the Flutter PaymentScreen — confirmed via:
     adb shell dumpsys activity activities | grep -i ResumedActivity
   -> topResumedActivity=...InAppBrowserActivity...
3. Pressed system back (adb shell input keyevent 4) to close the browser. dumpsys now shows MainActivity resumed (Flutter PaymentScreen, AppBar title "Payment").
4. Tapped the AppBar's "Back" arrow (content-desc "Back") -> triggers PaymentScreenState._exitApp().
   ui_list dump immediately after:
     Cancel Add Fund
     Dismiss
     Do you want to cancel this add fund?
   (FundPaymentDialogWidget, correct copy — matches this ticket's AND-logic parity check.)
5. Tapped "Cancel Add Fund" ONCE. ui_list dump immediately after — UNCHANGED, same 3 nodes:
     Cancel Add Fund
     Dismiss
     Do you want to cancel this add fund?
   (No navigation occurred; dialog reads as still on-screen with identical content.)
   userapp-run.log gained exactly 1 new line in this window (an unrelated Firebase Analytics
   warning "E/FA: Missing google_app_id..."), no [NET] POST order/cancel line, no [ERR]/[FAIL].
6. Tapped "Cancel Add Fund" a SECOND time (same coordinates via ui_tap "Cancel Add Fund").
   ui_list dump immediately after landed on the PROFILE screen (2 navigation levels back from
   Wallet, e.g. "ACCOUNT SETTINGS", "Wallet ⁦0.09 AED⁩", "Logout" etc. visible) — i.e. it skipped
   past the Wallet screen entirely, which a single clean Get.back(); Get.back(); (dialog + payment
   screen) should have landed on.

Assessment: matches an already-documented, previously LOW-CONFIDENCE / unconfirmed note in
docs/apps/userapp/userapp-navigation-guide.md ("Payment screen entry via Wallet Add Fund",
NEARS-2190/2346 QA, 2026-08-19): "exiting via the NAppBar's *unguarded* app-bar back arrow
followed by a tap of the dialog's own Cancel button occasionally left an orphaned duplicate
dialog stuck on top of the Wallet screen one level down, needing a second Cancel/barrier tap to
fully clear." This live repro reproduces that exact symptom shape (first tap absorbed/no-op,
second tap needed, and the eventual landing screen is one level further back than expected),
raising it from "low confidence, not reproduced" to reproduced-once this session.

Scope: this dialog-orchestration logic lives in payment_screen.dart / payment_back_guard.dart —
BOTH untouched by NEARS-2623's diff (which only edits payment_webview_screen.dart's _exitApp()
condition). Non-blocking to NEARS-2623's verdict; filed as a regression-candidate per QA process
(unrelated pre-existing issue), not a task_bug of this ticket.
